  "term": "Developmental Test of Visual–Motor Integration",
  "definition": "The Developmental Test of Visual–Motor Integration is an assessment used to measure visual-motor integration, or how well a child coordinates visual information with fine-motor responses. In the cited source, it is also used to assess related abilities such as visual perception and motor coordination.",
